WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:08.308 --> 00:00:11.177
For more than 40 years, CNN has offered

00:00:11.177 --> 00:00:11.978
a front row

00:00:11.978 --> 00:00:14.280
seat to history in the making.

00:00:15.015 --> 00:00:16.182
Why am I under arrest?

00:00:16.182 --> 00:00:17.851
It's a hoax set up.

00:00:17.851 --> 00:00:18.451
Join us

00:00:18.451 --> 00:00:20.720
as we turn back the clock to expose

00:00:21.054 --> 00:00:21.888
Osama bin Laden

00:00:21.888 --> 00:00:23.123
and watch the stories

00:00:23.123 --> 00:00:25.191
that have defined our time

00:00:25.191 --> 00:00:27.293
There are no words to say O.J.

00:00:27.293 --> 00:00:28.161
Simpson

00:00:30.497 --> 00:00:33.433
This is CNN's Rewind

00:00:35.802 --> 00:00:37.237
It was January 19.

00:00:37.237 --> 00:00:40.306
86 Americans had just been introduced

00:00:40.306 --> 00:00:41.574
to Nintendo.

00:00:41.574 --> 00:00:44.044
Back to the Future was in theaters

00:00:44.044 --> 00:00:45.178
and the Cold War

00:00:45.178 --> 00:00:47.414
was beginning to warm up.

00:00:47.414 --> 00:00:49.783
Meanwhile, NASA's shuttle program

00:00:49.783 --> 00:00:51.951
was bringing the dream of space travel

00:00:51.951 --> 00:00:53.453
closer to home.

00:00:53.653 --> 00:00:55.822
Here today to announce the first private

00:00:55.822 --> 00:00:56.956
citizen passenger

00:00:56.956 --> 00:00:58.958
in the history of space flight.

00:00:58.958 --> 00:01:01.027
But on a cold January morning,

00:01:01.361 --> 00:01:03.463
disaster would ground the ambitions

00:01:03.463 --> 00:01:05.632
of spaceflight for years to come

00:01:06.433 --> 00:01:08.935
to one and

00:01:19.312 --> 00:01:20.513
the space race began in

00:01:20.513 --> 00:01:22.482
earnest after World War Two.

00:01:22.482 --> 00:01:23.383
Both the United States

00:01:23.383 --> 00:01:24.250
and the Soviet Union

00:01:24.250 --> 00:01:26.052
perfected rockets and missiles

00:01:26.052 --> 00:01:26.786
from the beginning.

00:01:26.786 --> 00:01:28.054
The space program was more

00:01:28.054 --> 00:01:29.489
than a scientific experiment.

00:01:29.489 --> 00:01:31.091
It was a matter of national pride

00:01:31.091 --> 00:01:32.692
and national security.

00:01:32.692 --> 00:01:34.694
With the U.S. on top of the space race.

00:01:34.694 --> 00:01:36.362
Now, so let military considerations

00:01:36.362 --> 00:01:37.297
take a backseat

00:01:37.297 --> 00:01:39.065
and concentrated on science.

00:01:39.065 --> 00:01:40.100
But now Congress

00:01:40.100 --> 00:01:41.000
wanted a return

00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:42.435
on their space investment.

00:01:42.435 --> 00:01:43.503
Billions of dollars

00:01:43.503 --> 00:01:43.970
had been poured

00:01:43.970 --> 00:01:45.472
into the national project.

00:01:45.472 --> 00:01:47.173
The seventies found national researchers

00:01:47.173 --> 00:01:48.374
back to the drawing board,

00:01:48.374 --> 00:01:49.609
working almost nonstop

00:01:49.609 --> 00:01:51.611
to develop this space vehicle

00:01:51.611 --> 00:01:53.179
that could be launched into space

00:01:53.179 --> 00:01:55.682
and returned much like an airplane

00:01:55.682 --> 00:01:57.884
on November 24th. 1980.

00:01:57.884 --> 00:01:59.052
The first space shuttle

00:01:59.052 --> 00:02:00.353
rolled out of the hangar.

00:02:00.353 --> 00:02:01.988
Its name, Columbia.

00:02:01.988 --> 00:02:04.424
It marked a new era in space exploration.

00:02:04.757 --> 00:02:06.426
Since then, three other shuttle crafts

00:02:06.426 --> 00:02:07.127
have been built.

00:02:07.127 --> 00:02:09.229
Challenger, Discovery and Atlantis

00:02:25.044 --> 00:02:27.280
Today, I'm directing Nelson

00:02:27.280 --> 00:02:27.714
to begin

00:02:27.714 --> 00:02:28.781
a search

00:02:28.781 --> 00:02:30.183
in all of our elementary

00:02:30.183 --> 00:02:32.085
and secondary schools

00:02:32.085 --> 00:02:32.952
and to choose

00:02:32.952 --> 00:02:34.787
as the first citizen passionate

00:02:34.787 --> 00:02:35.889
passenger in the history

00:02:35.889 --> 00:02:37.657
of our space program.

00:02:37.657 --> 00:02:40.226
One of America's finest, a teacher

00:02:44.597 --> 00:02:45.465
applications

00:02:45.465 --> 00:02:47.233
to be the first civilian in space

00:02:47.233 --> 00:02:49.002
will be distributed through all U.S.

00:02:49.002 --> 00:02:51.271
public, private and parochial schools.

00:02:51.471 --> 00:02:53.039
Nassau officials will select

00:02:53.039 --> 00:02:54.474
one civilian astronaut

00:02:54.474 --> 00:02:55.608
and one backup

00:02:55.608 --> 00:02:57.877
for several months of preflight training.

00:02:58.311 --> 00:03:00.713
The teacher who will be going into space,

00:03:00.713 --> 00:03:03.683
Christa McAuliffe, first said, You

00:03:11.324 --> 00:03:13.059
make all of the space for training.

00:03:13.059 --> 00:03:15.061
She clearly relished the challenge.

00:03:15.195 --> 00:03:17.096
She said she hoped to inspire others

00:03:17.096 --> 00:03:17.797
to reach out

00:03:17.797 --> 00:03:20.099
and try new and different things.

00:03:20.533 --> 00:03:22.435
One of the things that I would like to do

00:03:22.435 --> 00:03:23.503
when I go aboard

00:03:23.503 --> 00:03:24.871
the shuttle is to bring

00:03:24.871 --> 00:03:26.339
back the wonder of it all.

00:03:29.275 --> 00:03:30.677
To see

00:03:31.044 --> 00:03:33.613
McAuliffe like a wrecking yard

00:03:33.613 --> 00:03:34.814
or something,

00:03:34.814 --> 00:03:37.083
you know, floating around in space

00:03:39.519 --> 00:03:40.753
First it was the wind.

00:03:40.753 --> 00:03:42.522
Then it was a frozen bolt.

00:03:42.522 --> 00:03:44.123
Then it was the wind again.

00:03:44.123 --> 00:03:45.291
As a result, the space

00:03:45.291 --> 00:03:46.993
shuttle Challenger is still sitting on

00:03:46.993 --> 00:03:48.361
launch pad 39 B

00:03:48.361 --> 00:03:49.896
at the Kennedy Space Center.

00:03:49.896 --> 00:03:51.331
The weather once again

00:03:51.331 --> 00:03:54.100
ruining NASA's show

00:03:59.806 --> 00:04:00.673
but the country's

00:04:00.673 --> 00:04:03.009
space agency has learned in recent weeks,

00:04:03.009 --> 00:04:04.410
as well as the rest of us, is

00:04:04.410 --> 00:04:05.545
that this is a difficult

00:04:05.545 --> 00:04:06.646
general time of year

00:04:06.646 --> 00:04:08.448
to try and launch a space shuttle.

00:04:08.448 --> 00:04:10.383
Patience has been a key element

00:04:10.383 --> 00:04:12.285
around the nascent operation

00:04:12.285 --> 00:04:13.186
all this week.

00:04:13.186 --> 00:04:13.753
We're going to join

00:04:13.753 --> 00:04:15.722
Tom Mintier now at once again

00:04:15.722 --> 00:04:17.123
just getting down about 3 minutes.

00:04:17.123 --> 00:04:18.091
And they think they can do it.

00:04:18.091 --> 00:04:19.125
They are counting.

00:04:19.125 --> 00:04:20.493
The ice is cleared away

00:04:20.493 --> 00:04:22.629
and Challenger should be going away

00:04:22.629 --> 00:04:23.730
very soon.

00:04:23.730 --> 00:04:25.098
Let's go down to the Kennedy Space Center

00:04:25.098 --> 00:04:26.165
and take a look at Challenger

00:04:26.165 --> 00:04:27.166
sitting on the pad

00:04:27.166 --> 00:04:29.102
as they continue the countdown.

00:04:29.102 --> 00:04:31.170
They started the auxiliary power units

00:04:31.170 --> 00:04:32.672
about a minute ago

00:04:32.672 --> 00:04:34.574
and that is one of the major

00:04:34.574 --> 00:04:37.777
milestones to continuing the countdown

00:04:37.844 --> 00:04:40.513
and counting. Gimble checks now complete

00:04:42.482 --> 00:04:43.082
U.S.

00:04:43.483 --> 00:04:44.450
military operations.

00:04:44.450 --> 00:04:45.852
They have external tank,

00:04:45.852 --> 00:04:48.221
liquid oxygen, pressurization has started

00:04:48.221 --> 00:04:49.722
and purging of the shuttle main

00:04:49.722 --> 00:04:50.990
engines is terminated.

00:04:50.990 --> 00:04:54.294
I hope it takes off this time.

00:04:56.763 --> 00:04:57.664
Let's go

00:04:58.498 --> 00:04:59.432
through some

00:05:05.538 --> 00:05:06.572
more checks now.

00:05:06.572 --> 00:05:07.573
Complete

00:05:11.577 --> 00:05:12.812
during the six days in space,

00:05:12.812 --> 00:05:14.681
the astronauts are going to release

00:05:14.681 --> 00:05:16.716
a $100 million satellite

00:05:17.016 --> 00:05:18.985
and another one called Haley Spartan

00:05:18.985 --> 00:05:20.586
that will study the comet.

00:05:20.586 --> 00:05:22.221
But the highlight on this mission

00:05:22.221 --> 00:05:23.623
is the including

00:05:23.623 --> 00:05:25.258
in the flight of Christa McAuliffe,

00:05:25.258 --> 00:05:26.592
a 37 year old high school

00:05:26.592 --> 00:05:28.261
social studies teacher from Concord

00:05:28.261 --> 00:05:28.861
New Hampshire.

00:05:28.861 --> 00:05:31.531
She will teach from space on Friday.

00:05:31.564 --> 00:05:33.800
Now, if they are able to get off today,

00:05:34.233 --> 00:05:37.403
they will have live coverage here on CNN

00:05:37.637 --> 00:05:38.071
of her

00:05:38.071 --> 00:05:38.871
giving lessons

00:05:38.871 --> 00:05:41.641
to students on the ground here helping.

00:05:42.141 --> 00:05:44.610
T-minus 15 seconds, please go.

00:05:44.977 --> 00:05:45.678
I want it to

00:05:47.113 --> 00:05:48.548
be known as cameras

00:05:48.548 --> 00:05:51.651
nine or eight, seven, six.

00:05:51.984 --> 00:05:54.220
We have main engine start

00:05:54.220 --> 00:05:57.190
for three, two, one.

00:05:57.890 --> 00:06:02.028
And lift on liftoff of the 25th space

00:06:02.028 --> 00:06:02.729
shuttle mission.

00:06:02.729 --> 00:06:05.665
And it has cleared the tower,

00:06:05.665 --> 00:06:08.301
a controlling program

00:06:08.301 --> 00:06:10.636
right on the challenger

00:06:11.304 --> 00:06:14.407
the good roll program confirmed

00:06:15.675 --> 00:06:18.745
Challenger now heading downrange

00:06:25.885 --> 00:06:26.652
Engines beginning

00:06:26.652 --> 00:06:30.857
throttling now now at 94% normal throttle

00:06:31.190 --> 00:06:34.560
for most of the plane 204%

00:06:35.428 --> 00:06:37.597
will throttle down to 65%

00:06:37.964 --> 00:06:38.831
shortly

00:06:42.268 --> 00:06:42.702
engines at

00:06:42.702 --> 00:06:44.537
65% three engines

00:06:44.537 --> 00:06:46.539
running normally three good fuel cells

00:06:46.539 --> 00:06:48.341
three good APUs

00:06:50.476 --> 00:06:53.413
velocity 257 feet per second altitude

00:06:53.413 --> 00:06:55.181
4.3 nautical miles downrange

00:06:55.181 --> 00:06:57.583
distance three nautical miles

00:07:00.853 --> 00:07:02.622
So the 25th space shuttle mission

00:07:02.622 --> 00:07:04.190
is now on the way.

00:07:04.190 --> 00:07:05.358
After more

00:07:05.358 --> 00:07:06.793
delays, the NASA cares

00:07:06.793 --> 00:07:08.294
to count this morning.

00:07:08.294 --> 00:07:09.162
That looked as though

00:07:09.162 --> 00:07:10.897
they were not going to be able to get off

00:07:13.032 --> 00:07:14.634
One minute, 15 seconds velocity.

00:07:14.634 --> 00:07:15.601
2900 feet per

00:07:15.601 --> 00:07:17.270
second altitude, nine nautical miles

00:07:17.270 --> 00:07:20.506
downrange, distance, seven nautical miles

00:07:33.753 --> 00:07:34.487
It looks like a couple

00:07:34.487 --> 00:07:37.590
of the solid rocket boosters

00:07:37.590 --> 00:07:39.826
blew away from the side of the shuttle

00:07:40.927 --> 00:07:42.962
in an explosion

00:07:49.335 --> 00:07:50.002
Flight controllers

00:07:50.002 --> 00:07:50.436
here are looking

00:07:50.436 --> 00:07:53.473
very carefully at the situation.

00:07:53.639 --> 00:07:56.709
Obviously, a major malfunction

00:08:01.013 --> 00:08:02.949
We have no downlink

00:08:12.758 --> 00:08:13.593
please.

00:08:14.560 --> 00:08:16.062
For instance,

00:08:19.065 --> 00:08:20.533
you have the explosion on tape.

00:08:20.533 --> 00:08:22.368
Yes. Hi.

00:08:22.668 --> 00:08:24.303
Oh, my goodness.

00:08:27.673 --> 00:08:28.608
We're awaiting word.

00:08:28.608 --> 00:08:30.610
They're holding their breath.

00:08:30.610 --> 00:08:32.945
Just I'm sure, as everyone else is.

00:08:33.379 --> 00:08:35.014
You saw just a few moments ago

00:08:35.014 --> 00:08:37.783
about 45 seconds after liftoff,

00:08:38.084 --> 00:08:40.219
a huge fireball in the sky.

00:08:41.153 --> 00:08:42.522
We have a report from the Flight

00:08:42.522 --> 00:08:43.356
Dynamics officer

00:08:43.356 --> 00:08:45.258
that the vehicle has exploded

00:08:45.258 --> 00:08:46.392
flight director confirms

00:08:46.392 --> 00:08:48.661
that we are looking at

00:08:48.661 --> 00:08:50.763
checking with the recovery forces to see

00:08:50.763 --> 00:08:51.898
what can be done at this point.

00:09:00.206 --> 00:09:01.741
Contingency procedures are

00:09:01.741 --> 00:09:03.109
in effect

00:09:08.114 --> 00:09:09.415
in what appears to be

00:09:09.415 --> 00:09:11.050
a major catastrophe

00:09:11.050 --> 00:09:13.152
in America's space program.

00:09:13.152 --> 00:09:14.053
Challenger

00:09:14.053 --> 00:09:15.187
only seconds

00:09:15.187 --> 00:09:17.323
after leaving the launch pad,

00:09:17.323 --> 00:09:18.124
according to NASA,

00:09:18.124 --> 00:09:20.226
has exploded in midair.

00:09:20.226 --> 00:09:21.127
No word yet on

00:09:21.127 --> 00:09:23.729
if there are any survivors.

00:09:23.729 --> 00:09:26.098
You can see what appears to be a ship

00:09:28.301 --> 00:09:31.337
off of the Kennedy Space Center.

00:09:31.504 --> 00:09:33.472
Just saw a splash in the water.

00:09:33.472 --> 00:09:35.007
Don't know if that was one of the solid

00:09:35.007 --> 00:09:38.044
rocket boosters or part of the

00:09:38.044 --> 00:09:39.011
shuttle

00:09:40.346 --> 00:09:42.615
on board the space shuttle this morning.

00:09:42.615 --> 00:09:44.717
Commander Francis Dick Scobee,

00:09:44.717 --> 00:09:47.620
copilot Michael Smith

00:09:47.620 --> 00:09:49.422
Judith Resnick,

00:09:49.655 --> 00:09:51.824
Ronald McNair,

00:09:52.325 --> 00:09:54.527
Jeffrey Jarvis and Christa McAuliffe

00:09:55.094 --> 00:09:57.196
and Ellison Azuka

00:09:57.196 --> 00:09:58.698
Let's take another look now.

00:09:58.698 --> 00:10:02.335
Just seconds, seconds into the launch.

00:10:02.335 --> 00:10:05.871
This is before the solid rockets were lit

00:10:07.139 --> 00:10:09.875
T-minus and go, man, or eight,

00:10:10.309 --> 00:10:12.044
seven, six.

00:10:12.044 --> 00:10:16.315
We have main engine start for 32,

00:10:16.682 --> 00:10:19.018
one, and liftoff.

00:10:19.485 --> 00:10:22.054
Liftoff of the 21st space

00:10:22.054 --> 00:10:22.755
shuttle mission.

00:10:22.755 --> 00:10:24.323
And it is clear as the tower

00:10:26.158 --> 00:10:28.394
controlling program

00:10:28.394 --> 00:10:30.663
right around the challenger

00:10:32.999 --> 00:10:35.434
control program confirmed

00:10:35.434 --> 00:10:39.071
the challenger now heading downrange

00:10:39.405 --> 00:10:40.773
Tom, everything looks normal

00:10:40.773 --> 00:10:41.974
to this point.

00:10:41.974 --> 00:10:43.175
I don't want to say it again.

00:10:43.175 --> 00:10:45.211
Everything looks normal to this point.

00:10:45.211 --> 00:10:45.578
It's one

00:10:45.578 --> 00:10:47.546
the long range tracking here on down now

00:10:47.546 --> 00:10:48.180
took over

00:10:48.180 --> 00:10:51.283
and you could see an extreme close up

00:10:51.450 --> 00:10:52.885
as the

00:10:53.052 --> 00:10:54.754
solid rocket boosters

00:10:54.754 --> 00:10:56.255
appeared to throttle down

00:10:56.255 --> 00:10:58.491
to be breaking away from the shuttle

00:10:58.491 --> 00:10:59.992
and then explode.

00:10:59.992 --> 00:11:02.995
It comes up in just a few seconds here

00:11:02.995 --> 00:11:04.030
and again,

00:11:04.597 --> 00:11:05.965
running normally

00:11:06.332 --> 00:11:06.899
there.

00:11:07.933 --> 00:11:08.467
You can see

00:11:08.467 --> 00:11:10.569
right before the explosion velocity,

00:11:10.569 --> 00:11:11.871
the external tank,

00:11:11.871 --> 00:11:13.506
it attaches to the shuttle.

00:11:13.506 --> 00:11:15.474
The flame appeared to break out

00:11:15.474 --> 00:11:17.076
between the external tank

00:11:17.076 --> 00:11:18.644
and the shuttle.

00:11:18.744 --> 00:11:19.045
Time.

00:11:19.045 --> 00:11:21.514
This has never happened before.

00:11:21.514 --> 00:11:22.615
I know you are aware

00:11:22.615 --> 00:11:24.950
that there are contingency plans for such

00:11:25.017 --> 00:11:25.785
such an event

00:11:26.719 --> 00:11:28.154
because it's never happened before.

00:11:28.154 --> 00:11:28.454
I think

00:11:28.454 --> 00:11:30.523
possibly many people even involved

00:11:30.523 --> 00:11:32.024
are not aware of what they are.

00:11:32.024 --> 00:11:34.493
Do they have ships standing by?

00:11:34.493 --> 00:11:36.295
There are recovery ships standing by

00:11:36.295 --> 00:11:38.264
and they do go through

00:11:38.264 --> 00:11:41.367
procedures for launch aborts.

00:11:41.967 --> 00:11:44.804
There is a worst case scenario.

00:11:45.604 --> 00:11:47.473
We have CNN's John Zarrella

00:11:47.473 --> 00:11:48.708
at the Kennedy Space Center

00:11:48.708 --> 00:11:50.743
on the live line now.

00:11:50.743 --> 00:11:51.977
John, you could,

00:11:51.977 --> 00:11:52.511
I'm sure,

00:11:52.511 --> 00:11:54.080
see it from your vantage point,

00:11:54.080 --> 00:11:55.514
even nine miles down.

00:11:55.514 --> 00:11:56.749
Describe the scene there.

00:11:56.749 --> 00:11:57.349
Here now

00:11:57.349 --> 00:11:58.951
it's at the Kennedy Space Center.

00:11:58.951 --> 00:12:00.486
Everybody is just stunned.

00:12:00.486 --> 00:12:01.921
They're in shock.

00:12:01.921 --> 00:12:02.922
It's a situation

00:12:02.922 --> 00:12:03.823
where people are just

00:12:03.823 --> 00:12:05.391
sort of standing around and,

00:12:05.391 --> 00:12:05.624
you know,

00:12:05.624 --> 00:12:07.226
just bewilderment at this point.

00:12:07.226 --> 00:12:07.693
And,

00:12:07.993 --> 00:12:08.527
of course,

00:12:08.527 --> 00:12:10.129
we're not getting any information

00:12:10.129 --> 00:12:11.097
from here

00:12:11.097 --> 00:12:13.199
any more than what you are, only

00:12:13.199 --> 00:12:14.834
just what we have just witnessed

00:12:14.834 --> 00:12:16.836
and what seen as tragic, tragic incident

00:12:17.770 --> 00:12:19.572
with the explosion that we saw

00:12:19.572 --> 00:12:20.473
just a few minutes ago.

00:12:20.473 --> 00:12:21.207
We're back now

00:12:21.207 --> 00:12:24.276
to a live picture from a helicopter above

00:12:25.010 --> 00:12:26.078
the launch area.

00:12:26.078 --> 00:12:28.247
This is Mission Control in Houston.

00:12:28.247 --> 00:12:30.182
For the last four or 5 minutes.

00:12:30.182 --> 00:12:31.650
The audio channel from Mission

00:12:31.650 --> 00:12:33.652
Control has been silent.

00:12:33.652 --> 00:12:35.788
Not a single word has been spoken.

00:12:35.788 --> 00:12:37.323
While the rescue efforts,

00:12:37.323 --> 00:12:38.390
if there are any to be

00:12:38.390 --> 00:12:40.726
made, are underway.

00:12:40.726 --> 00:12:41.560
Let's go to the White House

00:12:41.560 --> 00:12:43.496
now and Larry speaks and shocked

00:12:43.496 --> 00:12:46.665
at what he is just seeing replayed

00:12:46.665 --> 00:12:47.533
on television

00:12:47.533 --> 00:12:49.769
concerning the shuttle launch.

00:12:49.769 --> 00:12:52.238
We do not have any more information

00:12:52.238 --> 00:12:53.506
than it is being provided to the

00:12:53.506 --> 00:12:54.774
public at this time.

00:12:56.208 --> 00:12:57.309
The way the first person

00:12:57.309 --> 00:12:58.511
found out about it is

00:12:58.511 --> 00:13:01.080
he was in the Oval Office.

00:13:01.213 --> 00:13:02.214
The vice president

00:13:02.214 --> 00:13:04.049
and the foreign policy adviser,

00:13:04.049 --> 00:13:06.819
John Poindexter, came in with others

00:13:07.052 --> 00:13:08.254
and informed the president

00:13:08.254 --> 00:13:10.556
that the news had just broken.

00:13:10.556 --> 00:13:11.190
We immediately

00:13:11.190 --> 00:13:12.424
adjourned our Oval Office

00:13:12.424 --> 00:13:15.060
meeting and went into an adjoining room.

00:13:15.060 --> 00:13:16.395
The president study

00:13:16.395 --> 00:13:17.997
where there's a television.

00:13:17.997 --> 00:13:20.099
And the president then began to review

00:13:20.099 --> 00:13:24.103
television reports of the explosion there

00:13:24.103 --> 00:13:25.604
shortly after the launch.

00:13:25.604 --> 00:13:26.238
So once again,

00:13:26.238 --> 00:13:28.541
the president is as concerned.

00:13:28.974 --> 00:13:31.243
He is is is saddened.

00:13:31.243 --> 00:13:33.445
He is very anxious

00:13:33.445 --> 00:13:35.514
to have more information on it

00:13:35.514 --> 00:13:37.016
at the moment, as I say,

00:13:37.016 --> 00:13:38.884
we're learning most of our information

00:13:38.884 --> 00:13:40.753
from what the public is getting

00:13:40.753 --> 00:13:41.287
everything said

00:13:41.287 --> 00:13:41.787
about the fact

00:13:41.787 --> 00:13:43.789
that the teacher was on board this plane.

00:13:43.789 --> 00:13:45.357
Well, it was something that was

00:13:45.357 --> 00:13:47.493
it was on all of our minds that

00:13:47.493 --> 00:13:49.528
that we did have the first teacher

00:13:49.528 --> 00:13:51.297
in space, really, the first

00:13:52.531 --> 00:13:53.232
civilian, so

00:13:53.232 --> 00:13:53.766
to speak,

00:13:53.766 --> 00:13:55.234
other than our members of Congress

00:13:55.234 --> 00:13:57.069
who have flown in space.

00:13:57.069 --> 00:13:58.671
And it certainly that's on our mind.

00:13:58.671 --> 00:14:00.506
Tom, we've just learned from a

00:14:00.506 --> 00:14:01.273
wire report

00:14:01.273 --> 00:14:02.875
that the students at Christa McAuliffe

00:14:02.875 --> 00:14:04.143
High School in New Hampshire

00:14:04.143 --> 00:14:05.311
were watching the lift off,

00:14:05.311 --> 00:14:06.645
along with hundreds of thousands

00:14:06.645 --> 00:14:07.880
of other Americans.

00:14:07.880 --> 00:14:09.515
Students filled the Concord High School

00:14:09.515 --> 00:14:11.717
Auditorium to watch the launch.

00:14:11.717 --> 00:14:13.252
As Challenger lifted off,

00:14:13.252 --> 00:14:15.754
they shouted Clap Blue horns.

00:14:15.754 --> 00:14:17.923
At first, few realized what had happened.

00:14:18.224 --> 00:14:19.925
Then the fact that what began

00:14:19.925 --> 00:14:20.860
as a joyous event

00:14:20.860 --> 00:14:22.294
had turned to tragedy hit them.

00:14:22.294 --> 00:14:24.163
They said on TV that it blew up

00:14:24.163 --> 00:14:25.364
and everybody started crying.

00:14:25.364 --> 00:14:28.267
And that's when I

00:14:28.334 --> 00:14:29.869
realized what happened.

00:14:29.869 --> 00:14:32.104
The word of the Challenger catastrophe

00:14:32.104 --> 00:14:33.138
struck Washington

00:14:33.138 --> 00:14:34.540
like a winter thunderbolt.

00:14:34.540 --> 00:14:35.941
The House of Representatives

00:14:35.941 --> 00:14:37.376
was in session

00:14:37.376 --> 00:14:39.912
at 1138 Eastern Time this morning,

00:14:40.246 --> 00:14:41.280
but not for long.

00:14:41.280 --> 00:14:41.714
The House

00:14:41.714 --> 00:14:43.249
chaplain and very quickly

00:14:43.249 --> 00:14:44.950
upon learning of the news,

00:14:44.950 --> 00:14:46.886
offered a prayer for those off

00:14:46.886 --> 00:14:48.420
the coast of Florida.

00:14:48.420 --> 00:14:52.024
James Ford presented the wishes

00:14:52.024 --> 00:14:53.025
and the will of the House

00:14:53.025 --> 00:14:54.827
to a chilled and cold

00:14:54.827 --> 00:14:56.061
House of Representatives.

00:14:58.497 --> 00:14:59.431
And at this special

00:14:59.431 --> 00:15:02.468
moment, let us remember in silent prayer,

00:15:03.569 --> 00:15:05.671
those who were involved in the spacecraft

00:15:05.671 --> 00:15:06.472
shuttle accident

00:15:06.472 --> 00:15:09.108
just a few minutes ago of Florida.

00:15:09.909 --> 00:15:11.210
Let us pray

00:15:13.012 --> 00:15:15.047
then the speaker, Tip O'Neill, a drive.

00:15:15.047 --> 00:15:16.382
When we come back to you,

00:15:16.382 --> 00:15:17.783
I want to take a pause

00:15:17.783 --> 00:15:19.551
for 10 seconds of silence.

00:15:19.551 --> 00:15:20.152
We'll go to what,

00:15:20.152 --> 00:15:22.154
a 14 and 10 seconds of silence

00:15:22.154 --> 00:15:23.022
and you can say that

00:15:23.022 --> 00:15:24.456
if you want challenger

00:15:24.456 --> 00:15:25.557
as far as it affects

00:15:25.557 --> 00:15:26.458
the nation's capital.

00:15:26.458 --> 00:15:27.526
Now, Bob,

00:15:29.295 --> 00:15:30.262
thank you, Richard.

00:15:30.262 --> 00:15:32.064
And we will pause now

00:15:32.064 --> 00:15:35.301
at CNN in our coverage for 10 seconds

00:15:35.301 --> 00:15:36.402
of silence

00:16:06.832 --> 00:16:08.300
3 minutes before launch time.

00:16:08.300 --> 00:16:09.134
Correspondent

00:16:09.134 --> 00:16:10.002
Tom Mintier

00:16:10.002 --> 00:16:11.470
joined us on the set

00:16:11.470 --> 00:16:14.540
to begin our live coverage of the launch

00:16:14.540 --> 00:16:16.141
of the only concern that

00:16:16.141 --> 00:16:16.775
that Nasser

00:16:16.775 --> 00:16:17.409
really showed

00:16:17.409 --> 00:16:19.678
this morning was with the icicles,

00:16:19.678 --> 00:16:20.879
some of them two foot long

00:16:20.879 --> 00:16:23.382
and it might be proper to go back

00:16:23.782 --> 00:16:24.249
and look

00:16:24.249 --> 00:16:26.518
and think about the situation with that.

00:16:26.785 --> 00:16:27.987
They were very concerned.

00:16:27.987 --> 00:16:29.521
They called an emergency meeting

00:16:29.521 --> 00:16:31.256
at the John

00:16:31.256 --> 00:16:33.459
Kennedy Space Center to discuss

00:16:33.459 --> 00:16:36.161
whether the ice on the pad area

00:16:36.161 --> 00:16:37.730
could possibly damage

00:16:37.730 --> 00:16:39.765
the shuttle on liftoff.

00:16:39.865 --> 00:16:41.667
NASA's has never gone through ice

00:16:41.667 --> 00:16:43.736
in the launch pad area before.

00:16:43.736 --> 00:16:46.005
And they decided at that meeting

00:16:46.138 --> 00:16:48.207
that it posed no danger

00:16:48.474 --> 00:16:50.342
and they went ahead with the countdown

00:16:50.342 --> 00:16:51.477
Associate Administrator

00:16:51.477 --> 00:16:53.712
Jess, more previously,

00:16:53.712 --> 00:16:55.147
when pressured about Nasser

00:16:55.147 --> 00:16:55.881
being so far

00:16:55.881 --> 00:16:56.815
behind schedule

00:16:56.815 --> 00:16:57.282
this year,

00:16:57.282 --> 00:16:59.351
already with two missions only flown

00:17:00.252 --> 00:17:02.588
stated emphatically that we will never

00:17:02.588 --> 00:17:05.824
compromise safety standards for schedule.

00:17:07.192 --> 00:17:09.361
Those were his words,

00:17:09.428 --> 00:17:11.997
just a few days ago.

00:17:11.997 --> 00:17:12.831
Charles, of course,

00:17:12.831 --> 00:17:14.767
the president has a public duty

00:17:14.767 --> 00:17:15.868
to perform tonight

00:17:15.868 --> 00:17:17.736
his State of the Union address at nine

00:17:17.736 --> 00:17:19.138
Eastern Time.

00:17:19.138 --> 00:17:21.306
It seems does it not almost inevitable

00:17:21.306 --> 00:17:22.808
that this is going to cast

00:17:22.808 --> 00:17:24.143
a long and mournful

00:17:24.143 --> 00:17:25.911
shadow over even that?

00:17:25.911 --> 00:17:27.613
Well, the president had hoped to make

00:17:27.613 --> 00:17:28.514
the kind of speech

00:17:28.514 --> 00:17:29.715
that it was being described

00:17:29.715 --> 00:17:32.951
here as a visionary, laying out his hopes

00:17:32.951 --> 00:17:33.919
for this country

00:17:33.919 --> 00:17:35.954
through the end to the next century.

00:17:36.455 --> 00:17:39.792
I think it is fair to guess, in fact, Mr.

00:17:39.792 --> 00:17:40.993
Speaker, sort of indicated

00:17:40.993 --> 00:17:42.561
that the president would be compelled

00:17:42.561 --> 00:17:44.263
to have something to say

00:17:44.263 --> 00:17:45.330
about this tragedy.

00:17:45.330 --> 00:17:46.832
And I think we will hear that tonight.

00:17:46.832 --> 00:17:47.366
Yes, it does

00:17:47.366 --> 00:17:49.334
indeed cast a pall on this event.

00:17:49.334 --> 00:17:51.236
And among the Americans

00:17:51.236 --> 00:17:52.905
who saw the devastation

00:17:52.905 --> 00:17:55.007
that struck America's space program

00:17:55.007 --> 00:17:56.375
and seven people aboard

00:17:56.375 --> 00:17:56.742
the space

00:17:56.742 --> 00:17:59.144
shuttle were the husband of 37 year

00:17:59.144 --> 00:18:00.512
old New Hampshire schoolteacher

00:18:00.512 --> 00:18:01.647
Christa McAuliffe

00:18:01.647 --> 00:18:03.248
and her nine year old daughter

00:18:04.216 --> 00:18:06.852
also at the Cape, or just actually three

00:18:06.852 --> 00:18:08.420
and a half miles from the Cape,

00:18:08.420 --> 00:18:10.589
watching as it happened this morning,

00:18:10.889 --> 00:18:12.624
where Christa McAuliffe,

00:18:12.624 --> 00:18:14.827
two parents, Edward and Grace Corrigan,

00:18:14.827 --> 00:18:16.662
were watching from a VIP area

00:18:16.662 --> 00:18:18.597
some three and a half miles away.

00:18:18.597 --> 00:18:20.299
The wire services are reported

00:18:20.299 --> 00:18:21.500
to observing, the two of them

00:18:21.500 --> 00:18:22.868
hugging and sobbing

00:18:22.868 --> 00:18:23.702
as they saw

00:18:23.702 --> 00:18:25.804
the explosion aboard the shuttle.

00:18:25.804 --> 00:18:27.406
These are the spectators

00:18:27.406 --> 00:18:29.041
that were watching

00:18:29.308 --> 00:18:29.975
shortly

00:18:31.643 --> 00:18:32.277
after

00:18:34.113 --> 00:18:34.179
that.

00:18:34.246 --> 00:18:36.348
65%, three engine running

00:18:36.348 --> 00:18:38.083
normally during the fuel cells,

00:18:38.083 --> 00:18:39.785
particularly the use

00:18:42.121 --> 00:18:42.488
three.

00:18:42.654 --> 00:18:44.723
253%. Now,

00:18:45.891 --> 00:18:47.993
this is raw, unedited video just

00:18:49.261 --> 00:18:51.763
sent via satellite

00:18:53.398 --> 00:18:55.534
They're just throwing up the

00:18:56.001 --> 00:18:57.202
challenger going.

00:18:57.202 --> 00:19:20.425
Right lot of pictures

00:19:20.425 --> 00:19:22.027
you were just seeing

00:19:22.027 --> 00:19:24.229
as Christa McAuliffe, the parents

00:19:24.229 --> 00:19:26.231
watching in horror.

00:19:26.365 --> 00:19:28.033
These are the students from her school

00:19:41.013 --> 00:19:42.247
here looking very

00:19:42.247 --> 00:19:44.883
carefully situation.

00:19:45.250 --> 00:19:48.053
Obviously literally unconscious.

00:19:48.487 --> 00:19:48.954
Many of them

00:19:48.954 --> 00:19:50.088
probably had their view blocked

00:19:50.088 --> 00:19:50.822
just as we did

00:19:50.822 --> 00:19:51.924
with the television cameras

00:19:51.924 --> 00:19:52.925
with just a

00:19:52.925 --> 00:19:55.694
huge fireball and a huge cloud of smoke.

00:19:56.562 --> 00:19:57.729
They may not realize yet

00:19:57.729 --> 00:19:59.097
what has happened.

00:19:59.565 --> 00:20:02.935
They go wherever

00:20:02.935 --> 00:20:04.937
you see concern etched on their faces,

00:20:06.338 --> 00:20:06.738
the breath

00:20:06.738 --> 00:20:09.675
that they've been holding released.

00:20:09.975 --> 00:20:13.178
And then the realization sets in

00:20:13.178 --> 00:20:15.147
that something is wrong

00:20:20.018 --> 00:20:23.288
I think that that shows

00:20:23.689 --> 00:20:25.591
you apart

00:20:25.624 --> 00:20:28.694
from on stage, you know, part

00:20:31.363 --> 00:20:31.763
yeah.

00:20:32.164 --> 00:20:32.731
At that point,

00:20:32.731 --> 00:20:34.566
all that remained will play dynamics.

00:20:34.566 --> 00:20:36.868
After that, the vehicle was exploded

00:20:36.868 --> 00:20:37.903
over into a commercial

00:20:37.903 --> 00:20:40.539
that we're looking at

00:20:40.539 --> 00:20:42.341
whether recovery process to see

00:20:42.341 --> 00:20:44.543
what can be done at that point.

00:20:51.750 --> 00:20:53.085
Simply as the procedures

00:20:53.085 --> 00:20:54.987
are so

00:21:00.092 --> 00:21:00.926
let's get it right

00:21:03.428 --> 00:21:05.430
or or at least feel

00:21:10.202 --> 00:21:10.535
the

00:21:12.304 --> 00:21:14.006
families of the astronauts

00:21:14.006 --> 00:21:16.141
normally in the grandstand

00:21:18.210 --> 00:21:18.277
And

00:21:19.244 --> 00:21:19.911
Tom, as John

00:21:19.911 --> 00:21:20.779
Zarrella pointed out

00:21:20.779 --> 00:21:21.980
from the cave earlier,

00:21:21.980 --> 00:21:25.183
when all of us first saw the blast

00:21:25.183 --> 00:21:26.485
and there was a moment of

00:21:26.485 --> 00:21:28.220
of stunned silence and disbelief,

00:21:28.220 --> 00:21:29.488
many people

00:21:29.588 --> 00:21:31.857
perhaps did confuse it with the.

00:21:32.190 --> 00:21:33.492
Is it the booster rock solid

00:21:33.492 --> 00:21:34.926
rocket booster separation?

00:21:34.926 --> 00:21:35.927
But it was a little later,

00:21:35.927 --> 00:21:37.296
it was far too early

00:21:37.296 --> 00:21:38.096
and far

00:21:38.096 --> 00:21:38.563
too big

00:21:38.563 --> 00:21:39.931
an explosion of

00:21:39.931 --> 00:21:42.167
Tom, the area that we were just watching.

00:21:42.267 --> 00:21:43.302
That is the VIP

00:21:43.302 --> 00:21:45.737
section, invited guests for this launch

00:21:46.471 --> 00:21:49.841
I myself received an invitation

00:21:49.841 --> 00:21:50.909
from Michael Smith,

00:21:50.909 --> 00:21:52.544
who was the pilot on this flight,

00:21:52.544 --> 00:21:54.713
to sit in these same bleachers

00:21:54.713 --> 00:21:56.748
and to watch his launch.

00:21:56.748 --> 00:21:58.083
Michael Smith has been a guest here

00:21:58.083 --> 00:22:00.552
on CNN before on our launch coverage.

00:22:00.819 --> 00:22:02.888
And he sent me a special invitation to go

00:22:03.088 --> 00:22:03.822
that would then

00:22:03.822 --> 00:22:05.791
include family members of the astronauts

00:22:05.791 --> 00:22:07.092
and it includes family

00:22:07.092 --> 00:22:08.727
members, schoolchildren

00:22:08.727 --> 00:22:11.263
from New Hampshire or

00:22:19.137 --> 00:22:20.339
ladies and gentlemen,

00:22:20.339 --> 00:22:20.906
I plan

00:22:20.906 --> 00:22:22.674
to speak to you tonight to report

00:22:22.674 --> 00:22:24.543
on the State of the Union

00:22:24.543 --> 00:22:25.510
for the events of earlier

00:22:25.510 --> 00:22:28.113
today have led me to change those plans.

00:22:29.081 --> 00:22:30.882
Today is a day for mourning

00:22:30.882 --> 00:22:32.384
and remembering

00:22:32.551 --> 00:22:35.020
19 years ago, almost to the day,

00:22:35.153 --> 00:22:36.655
we lost three astronauts

00:22:36.655 --> 00:22:39.124
in a terrible accident on the ground.

00:22:39.124 --> 00:22:40.292
But we've never lost

00:22:40.292 --> 00:22:42.160
an astronaut in flight.

00:22:42.160 --> 00:22:44.963
We've never had a tragedy like this.

00:22:44.963 --> 00:22:45.464
And perhaps

00:22:45.464 --> 00:22:46.665
we've forgotten the courage

00:22:46.665 --> 00:22:49.201
it took for the crew of the shuttle.

00:22:49.201 --> 00:22:50.602
But they the Challenger

00:22:50.602 --> 00:22:52.938
seven, were aware of the dangers,

00:22:52.938 --> 00:22:53.672
but overcame them

00:22:53.672 --> 00:22:56.174
and did their jobs brilliantly.

00:22:56.174 --> 00:22:58.410
We mourn seven heroes.

00:22:58.410 --> 00:23:00.579
We mourn their loss as a nation together.

00:23:01.646 --> 00:23:03.782
The families of the seven,

00:23:03.782 --> 00:23:05.283
we cannot bear, as you do,

00:23:05.283 --> 00:23:07.252
the full impact of this tragedy.

00:23:08.253 --> 00:23:09.621
But we feel the loss

00:23:09.621 --> 00:23:10.856
and we're thinking about you.

00:23:10.856 --> 00:23:12.591
So very much.

00:23:12.858 --> 00:23:15.827
Your loved ones were daring and brave,

00:23:15.827 --> 00:23:17.696
and they had that special grace,

00:23:17.696 --> 00:23:18.764
a special spirit

00:23:18.764 --> 00:23:20.632
that says, give me a challenge

00:23:20.632 --> 00:23:22.801
and I'll need it with joy.

00:23:22.801 --> 00:23:24.669
They had a hunger to explore the universe

00:23:24.669 --> 00:23:26.705
and discover its truths

00:23:26.705 --> 00:23:27.639
they wished to serve.

00:23:27.639 --> 00:23:29.107
And they did.

00:23:29.141 --> 00:23:31.276
They served all of us

00:23:31.443 --> 00:23:32.477
And I want to say something

00:23:32.477 --> 00:23:33.912
to the schoolchildren of America

00:23:33.912 --> 00:23:35.414
who were watching the live coverage

00:23:35.414 --> 00:23:37.716
of the shuttle's takeoff.

00:23:37.716 --> 00:23:39.151
I know it's hard to understand,

00:23:39.151 --> 00:23:40.652
but sometimes painful

00:23:40.652 --> 00:23:42.521
things like this happen.

00:23:42.521 --> 00:23:43.822
It's all part of the process

00:23:43.822 --> 00:23:46.458
of exploration and discovery.

00:23:46.458 --> 00:23:47.759
It's all part of

00:23:47.759 --> 00:23:48.627
taking a chance

00:23:48.627 --> 00:23:51.396
and expanding man's horizons.

00:23:51.396 --> 00:23:52.431
The future doesn't

00:23:52.431 --> 00:23:54.499
belong to the fainthearted.

00:23:54.499 --> 00:23:56.568
It belongs to the brave.

00:23:56.568 --> 00:23:57.536
The Challenger crew

00:23:57.536 --> 00:23:59.638
was pulling us into the future

00:23:59.638 --> 00:24:01.540
and we'll continue to follow them

00:24:07.712 --> 00:24:09.781
The shuttle's busiest schedule ever

00:24:10.048 --> 00:24:10.782
will be delayed

00:24:10.782 --> 00:24:11.917
while investigators

00:24:11.917 --> 00:24:14.653
figure out what went wrong

00:24:21.460 --> 00:24:22.661
The challenger would have flown

00:24:22.661 --> 00:24:24.262
successfully if the weather at Cape

00:24:24.262 --> 00:24:26.798
Canaveral had been warm.

00:24:29.835 --> 00:24:32.204
Massa was not communicating with itself

00:24:32.504 --> 00:24:34.206
and was keeping some problems

00:24:34.206 --> 00:24:37.075
secret from top management.

00:24:48.253 --> 00:24:49.521
Westbrook

00:24:49.921 --> 00:24:50.822
himself.

00:24:50.956 --> 00:24:53.158
There are no words today.

00:24:53.158 --> 00:24:53.992
History.

00:24:53.992 --> 00:24:55.293
United States.

00:24:55.293 --> 00:24:57.829
Osama bin Laden. Explosion.

00:24:57.829 --> 00:24:58.697
Donald Trump.

00:24:58.697 --> 00:25:00.932
Wins a hoax, etc..

00:25:00.932 --> 00:25:01.900
Why am I under arrest?

